    <briefdescription>
<para>Factory and registration helper for <ref refid="classthemis_1_1llamacpp_1_1_llama_cpp_plugin" kindref="compound">LlamaCppPlugin</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Provides static utilities to:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Create a raw <ref refid="classthemis_1_1llamacpp_1_1_llama_cpp_plugin" kindref="compound">LlamaCppPlugin</ref> (createPlugin)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Wrap it in an LLMPluginAdapter for use with the PluginManager (createAdapter)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Perform one-shot registration with LLMPluginManager (registerWithLLMManager)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Hot-plug lifecycle: <ref refid="classthemis_1_1llamacpp_1_1_llama_cpp_plugin" kindref="compound">LlamaCppPlugin</ref> can be registered with plugins::PluginManager via the LLMPluginAdapter. When the PluginManager hot-reloads the plugin (e.g. after a model file is replaced on disk), a reload listener can call registerReloadListener() to receive BEFORE_UNLOAD / AFTER_LOAD notifications and tear-down / re-initialise state accordingly.</para>
<para>Usage: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Simple:<sp/>register<sp/>with<sp/>LLMPluginManager</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>mgr<sp/>=<sp/>themis::llm::LLMPluginManager::instance();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1llamacpp_1_1_llama_cpp_plugin_registrar_1a2974c5ba95d52a76f2b179e8cf5fddb7" kindref="member">LlamaCppPluginRegistrar::registerWithLLMManager</ref>(mgr,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;llama_cpp&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>{});</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Advanced:<sp/>create<sp/>an<sp/>adapter<sp/>for<sp/>PluginManager</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>adapter<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="classthemis_1_1llamacpp_1_1_llama_cpp_plugin_registrar_1a1e573a0c67f5d4d7176a3dc3b1461429" kindref="member">LlamaCppPluginRegistrar::createAdapter</ref>({});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
